{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis","id":660807,"title":"Batman = Ugallu Nemesis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-11T09:45:27-07:00","id":660807,"title":"Batman = Ugallu Nemesis","content":"What the subject said. Discuss.<br /> Bonus round: Joker = Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:59:17-07:00","id":660830,"title":"","content":"That's the most common argument I've heard, though I imagine you could also stat him as an Eshmaki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T10:18:50-07:00","id":660850,"title":"","content":"Nah, Joker isn't a Hero. He's probably a Namtaru Ravager. Joker has no motivation or plans beyond &quot;kill everyone and everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> Batman believes that in its heart, mankind is good and those who turn to evil do so because events in their lives have drove them to it. He doesn't kill people because he honestly believes they can be redeemed through proper effort and treatment.<br /> <br /> Joker, on the other hand, believes that mankind is naturally evil and all it takes is one bad event to set the gears in motion.<br /> <br /> Batman and Joker don't kill each other because they are polar opposites. Batman wants to prove his ideals by successfully reforming the Joker, and conversely the Joker wants to prove his ideals by driving Batman over the edge. As long as one of them is alive, it gives the other something to continue fighting for. If either of them killed the other, it would prove they could not be corrupted / rehabilitated and thus their ideals would be flawed or even completely wrong.<br /> <br /> Batman and Joker need each other. In a way, they're kind of like broodmates who have a very intense rivalry with one another. <i>They're frenemies.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T12:10:49-07:00","id":660959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis?p=660830#post660830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the most common argument I've heard, though I imagine you could also stat him as an Eshmaki.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's fair. I'm mostly going off the version from the Arkham ________ series of games, where you could make a pretty good case for Anakim, too, as he pretty regularly beats the crap out of 20+ guys, some of whom are way bigger and stronger than him, often times ripping the weapons out of their hands and breaking them in front of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T15:26:59-07:00","id":661148,"title":"","content":"Honestly in the Arkham Series of Games he's Different Families based on which game your in...<br /> In Asylum he's a Ugallu what with the heavier mechanics of Stealth, and Limited Stalking/Praying on Crooks.<br /> In City he's Eshmaki, Reminding the criminals they are Prey/that even they have something to fear.<br /> In Knight he's Anakim, Going all out and Making sure that they KNOW who's Boss.<br /> (Also by the Time of Knight he's become a Literal Nightmare if the 100% ending is to be believed)<br /> <br /> In other Musings... Big Boss from MGS5 is... An Incarnate Beast (Either Anakim or Namtaru) Who's Taking alot (and i mean ALOT) of Beast's under his wings and raising them in a place that they can be safe (Motherbase)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T07:46:18-07:00","id":741741,"title":"","content":"What Kinship Nightmares would be based on Batman and Joker? Maybe they can make do with the ones already available. Batman uses &quot;You Deserve This&quot; on criminals because of his parents' death and resentment thereof, despite wanting criminals to be cured and have another chance. He also uses &quot;You Are Not Alone&quot; when investigating and stalking criminals. &quot;We Know All Your Secrets&quot; helps with detective work.<br /> <br /> Joker wants people to be nihilistic like him and not know who they really are (&quot;I prefer my past to be multiple choice!&quot; and &quot;Would you like to know which of your friends were coawrds?&quot;), so he uses &quot;Everything You Do Is Worthless&quot; and &quot;Tabula Rasa&quot;, with added psychological torture.<br /> <br /> Both of them use &quot;Behold, My True Form!&quot;, whether it's to show a bat-like or clown-like monstrosity. And that's if their Horrors really do resemble their human forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T08:10:32-07:00","id":744496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoragoSolitude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis?p=660959#post660959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's fair. I'm mostly going off the version from the Arkham ________ series of games, where you could make a pretty good case for Anakim, too, as he pretty regularly beats the crap out of 20+ guys, some of whom are way bigger and stronger than him, often times ripping the weapons out of their hands and breaking them in front of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the Anakim are the fear of being powerless and Batman has gotten his ass kicked plenty of times. He's not the invincible warrior everybody hypes him up to be. In fact, during Batman Year 1, he tried to fight crime without his suit and gadgets and street level punks almost killed him.<br /> <br /> I would place Batman somewhere in the category of either a Namtaru (scaring people with his appearance) or an Ugallu (Swooping down from the rooftops). I don't believe Eshmaki is appropriate because they represent the fear of being alone, and most of the criminals he goes after tend to travel in gangs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually I'm going to say original batman (Bruce) is a Namtaru, while new Batman (Terry) is an Ugallu.<br /> <br /> Old Batman can't fly, and he's afraid of bats, yet chose to dress up as one and become one with his fear. Plus he has the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EENaoUiLfV0\" target=\"_blank\">Batman Glare</a>.<br /> <br /> New Batman can fly and spends a lot of time traveling in the bat jet, so he's more prone to attack from the sky!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2015, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T11:31:40-07:00","id":744757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Eshmaki is appropriate because they represent the fear of being alone, and most of the criminals he goes after tend to travel in gangs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course, I believe they also represent fear of darkness, sudden violence, and the thing that's there but you can't see. Not to mention that many Batmans have a knack for picking off enemies one by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T12:10:02-07:00","id":744794,"title":"","content":"Batman doesn't always solve problems with sneak attacks. He is mainly a detective, and sometimes doesn't engage in the combat directly. Also, the Birthright of the Ugallu is excellent for revealing hidden things, which is a great advantage for a detective (not that Batman's mundane investigative skills are lacking). Besides, I find the nickname of &quot;Dragons&quot; for the Eshmaki and their Dragonfire Atavism a bit ill-fitting with the whole Darkness theme. He does have the &quot;From The Shadows&quot; and &quot;Relentless Hunter&quot; Atavisms, though. I'd say Batman is indeed an Ugallu, as shown by his famous ability to overcome his enemies' powers and protections with prep time. Finally, he has a winged Horror, complete with &quot;Wings Of The Raptor&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T14:48:15-07:00","id":745168,"title":"","content":"Another idea is that Joker is the Begotten and he forms Family Ties with the other critters thrown into Arkham with him. This makes the Hero that Batman is (and he has developed a ton of Merits to aid him, even the supernatural ones) to be even more effective. Why, do you ask? Because the Joker is an Incarnate Beast itself. He used the others to strike at the Hero and to buff them when he could in hopes to create even more chaos. The more chaos, then the easier it would be to subvert Batman. But he does not want them to take down Batman. No. that is for the Joker to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T16:06:28-07:00","id":745298,"title":"","content":"As Nyrufa mentioned, Joker is probably a Ravager, though he could also have Tyrant as his second Hunger, seeing as how he's known as &quot;The Clown Prince Of Crime&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for his Family, you could go multiple ways. Namtaru does fit. It is said many people fear clowns because they look like dead and deformed people to our subconscious, with their pale skins and bloated noses. Namtaru!Joker's Horror might look like a psychedelic zombie straight out of a Nurgle army, and he painted his human form to vaguely resemble his Horror.<br /> <br /> However, you could say that he is a Makara. In this case, the &quot;Depths&quot; do not refer to the sea nor the earth, but to the mind, and the dark things found within. The Makara are said to often possesses hidden or sunken knowledge, as do some madmen who might be called visionaries from the right angle. The water in his Chamber based on the chemical plant where he used to work isn't water at all, but a mix of Lair Traits that mimics the effects of the Joker Venom. When people feel like they are &quot;drowning&quot; due to the effect of his Birthright, that could be the Joker Venom following him around like a noxious gas. He might have used Alien Allure to make Harley his sidekick, or he might have even Devoured her. His Poker Cards are custom made to be coated with the poison created by the Basilisk's Touch Atavism. Despite all of this, I still think Joker focuses on Family Dinners with the other Batman villains and very special feedings (see Barbara's fate in &quot;The Killing Joke&quot;) to keep his Satiety high and improve his Nightmares. That gives him an edge when trying to drive people mad. His Horror in this case would look different. The strands of his hair become green tentacles, his skin becomes pale like that of an eel, his eyes glow like the lure of an angler fish, and his smile turns very, very shark-like, all dripping with blood. I like this version better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-31-2015, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:37:58-07:00","id":745436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis?p=745168#post745168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea is that Joker is the Begotten and he forms Family Ties with the other critters thrown into Arkham with him. This makes the Hero that Batman is (and he has developed a ton of Merits to aid him, even the supernatural ones) to be even more effective. Why, do you ask? Because the Joker is an Incarnate Beast itself. He used the others to strike at the Hero and to buff them when he could in hopes to create even more chaos. The more chaos, then the easier it would be to subvert Batman. But he does not want them to take down Batman. No. that is for the Joker to do.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I am very fond of the idea of the Joker as an Incarnate (my other favorite interpretation is a Maniac Slasher), I can't see Batman as a Hero. Batman's most important rule is not killing, and he even refrains from killing the Joker when it would have stopped a whole lot of chaos and destruction. A Hero who got the chance would never do that, they feel nothing but hatred for Beasts. Furthermore, Batman works quite well with other superheroes when need be, despite keeping kryptonite and the like stored away just in case a member of the Justice League turns evil. If Batman is not an Ugallu or another supernatural, he is an epic Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-31-2015, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:31:29-08:00","id":747973,"title":"","content":"I hadn't considered the possibility of a Makara Joker, but it makes perfect sense now!<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also say that in his own way the Anakim would also be fitting. Joker is the one opponent who does not fear Batman. He actually laughs his ass off when he's getting beat to within an inch of his life and after Batman leaves him in a body cast for six months, he has the balls to remind him about his dead sidekick and ask if he's just going to leave him in another cast when Batman gets angry. The Joker can not be intimidated, he's become a man with nothing else to lose. Everybody knows how extremely dangerous that kind of person can be when they're your enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:26:32-08:00","id":750312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis?p=747973#post747973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't considered the possibility of a Makara Joker, but it makes perfect sense now!<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also say that in his own way the Anakim would also be fitting. Joker is the one opponent who does not fear Batman. He actually laughs his ass off when he's getting beat to within an inch of his life and after Batman leaves him in a body cast for six months, he has the balls to remind him about his dead sidekick and ask if he's just going to leave him in another cast when Batman gets angry. The Joker can not be intimidated, he's become a man with nothing else to lose. Everybody knows how extremely dangerous that kind of person can be when they're your enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Most Anakim render people powerless through physical supremacy, but that's not how the Joker does it. People are powerless to predict and stop his sadistic plans because he is mad beyond all reckoning, his insanity as deep and dark as the bottom of the ocean. His henchmen do the heavy fighting for him. Besides, he's a poor combatant more often than not. He's much more likely to just shoot you if you don't stab your pet cat to death, or catch you off guard and &quot;pull a magic trick&quot;. In a one-on-one fight against normal people, he wins not because of formal training in martial arts, but because <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PowerBornOfMadness\" target=\"_blank\"><b>he has no regard for his opponent's life or even his own.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:57:02-08:00","id":750364,"title":"","content":"In thinking about this.. batman as a beast.... actually brings the rest of the bat family into perspective. He may have been the one who was responsible for most of the various robins' devouring. The bat girls, and bat women may have been spontaneous devourings, but they were all brought into Batman's brood. In fact.. many of the characters in batman make a whole heck of a lot of sense as beasts (with a sprinkling of mages, changelings, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:53:26-08:00","id":752416,"title":"","content":"<b>Namtaru:</b> Two Face, Penguin, Scarecrow, Hush<br /> <br /> <b>Anakim:</b> Clayface, Killer Croc, Bane<br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu:</b> Firefly, Manbat<br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki:</b> Red Hood, Mr. Freeze, Harley Quin<br /> <br /> <b>Makara:</b> Joker, Poison Ivy(?), Hugo Strange, Ra's Al Ghul(?)<br /> <br /> <br /> That sound good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:35:42-08:00","id":752543,"title":"","content":"Ivy is just to good to pass up as a changeling IMHO &gt;_&gt;; and Ra's is difficult to place in general... but yeah.. sounds pretty good elsewise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:26:02-08:00","id":753107,"title":"","content":"Well Ra's is the leader of an organization of assassins and he's prolonged his life with the aid of the Lazarus pit. I figured ancient secrets and water seemed to fit him. I would place his Hunger as a Punisher, since he honestly believes that he is making the world a better place by targeting the weak and corrupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}